      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "fuel"
        ],
        "note": "2,158 rows, read for TWO columns. `fuelSubtypeID` is the link from a supplied formulation to the fuel type it is a formulation OF, which is what `sulfatefractions` keys on through `fuelsubtype`. `sulfurLevel` is the sulfate fraction's own argument (sulfate_pm_calculator.rs:838-841): the adjustment is 1 + BaseFuelSulfateFraction x (sulfurLevel / BaseFuelSulfurLevel - 1), and the three formulations this county is supplied carry 7.15, 6.00 and 7.15 ppm against base levels of 161.2, 172.0, 23.5 and 11.0 -- so the adjustment is far from 1 and is the single most load-bearing factor in the chain (docs/process-pm-exhaust.md 7.2, row 18). `sulfurLevel` is NULL-as-zero in MOVES and non-null on all three. The oxygenate volumes, RVP, T50/T90 and the aromatic and biodiesel contents are NOT read: they are `FuelEffectsGenerator`'s arguments, and this fixture is on the snapshot path where `generalfuelratio` ships already evaluated (docs/process-pm-exhaust.md 8.3).",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
