          "fuelEffectRatio",
          "fuelEffectRatioGPA"
        ]
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_generalfuelratio"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "fuel",
          "adjustment"
        ],
        "note": "58 rows, and they carry TWO pollutants that enter the chain at TWO DIFFERENT STAGES. The polProcessID 11201 rows are the elemental-carbon fuel effect and are applied by `BaseRateCalculator` (adjust.rs:452-472): per SUPPLIED formulation, blended by the county GPA fraction, under an inclusive model-year band AND an inclusive age band. The 12001 rows are the residue's, and are applied inside `SulfatePMCalculator` (SulfatePMCalculator.sql 75 restricts its own extract to `gfr.pollutantID in (120)`): raw, not GPA-blended, not per formulation, and as an UPDATE rather than a join, so a miss leaves the value alone. Six of the 58 rows reach source type 21 -- 1.090910749585 on gasoline and E85 of model year 2001 or later, 0.9727 on diesel of 2006 or earlier -- and applying both stages to one quantity would SQUARE the 1.0909 (../moves.rs records that trap at sulfate_pm_calculator.rs:2226). Pollutant 120 is INTERNAL to `SulfatePMCalculator` and never reaches `BaseRateCalculator`, which is why the two stages cannot be merged.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
