        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "pm_runspecpollutantprocess": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-pm-exhaust/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecpollutantprocess.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecpollutantprocess"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope"
        ],
        "note": "7 rows: 11201 (elemental carbon) and 11801 (composite NonECPM), which are the two RATED pollutant-processes, plus 11501 (sulfate particulate), 11901 (H2O aerosol), 11101 (organic carbon), 11001 (PM2.5 total) and 10001 (PM10 total), which are computed from them. It is the only place the run's pollutant/process scope is written down; it comes from here and never from the RunSpec XML. It is not an output-block axis: the output relation is ranked globally over the rate relation (docs/esm-conventions.md 31) and this relation's ordinal reaches the output row through the rate row instead. All seven blocks are the same 104 cohorts, which no earlier multi-pollutant rung could say.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "pm_runspecchainedto": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-pm-exhaust/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__runspecchainedto.parquet"
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_runspecchainedto"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "scope",
          "chain"
        ],
        "note": "8 rows, and they are CYCLIC: 11801 <- 11501 and 11501 <- 11801, 11801 <- 11901 and 11901 <- 11801. `SulfatePMCalculator` splits composite NonECPM into sulfate, water and an internal residue and then RE-SUMS NonECPM from them, so MOVES's chain table records both directions and cannot distinguish an input from an output. The fixed-point iteration docs/esm-conventions.md 32.1 introduced for `process-airtoxics` therefore DOES NOT TERMINATE on this table, and no `rspp_rootPolProcessID` is computed: the arithmetic comes from sulfate_pm_calculator.rs's stages, which are a DAG. What the table is read for is one row-set fact that IS cycle-free -- 11201 appears only as an input and every other selected pollutant-process appears as an output, so `run_unchainedPolProcessCount` is 1 while TWO blocks are rated. That gap is the measurement: MOVES's chain declaration cannot identify the rated set here.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "pm_sulfatefractions": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-pm-exhaust/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__sulfatefractions.parquet"
      },
      "reader_options": {
        "float_columns": [
          "SulfatenonECPMFraction",
          "H2OnonECPMFraction",
          "BaseFuelSulfurLevel",
          "BaseFuelSulfateFraction"
        ]
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_sulfatefractions"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "pm",
          "speciation"
        ],
        "note": "6 rows: two model-year bands for each of fuel types 1, 2 and 5 at source type 21, and NO fuel-type-9 row -- which is the first of the two independent misses that empty the twenty electricity cohorts (docs/process-pm-exhaust.md 2.7). It carries FOUR numbers per band and they are used in two different ways. `SulfatenonECPMFraction` and `H2OnonECPMFraction` are the base fractions of composite NonECPM; `BaseFuelSulfurLevel` and `BaseFuelSulfateFraction` are the sulfur sensitivity that scales them (sulfate_pm_calculator.rs:838-841). THE ADJUSTED FRACTION GOES TO SULFATE AND THE UNADJUSTED ONE TO THE RESIDUE, so the split does not conserve mass -- 0.8385 to 0.9865 of the parent over this run's six cells -- and that asymmetry is the most load-bearing detail in the rung. `H2OnonECPMFraction` is 0 on all six rows, so pollutant 119 is 208 rows of exactly zero and the water term of the residue fraction never leaves the sulfate term (docs/process-pm-exhaust.md 7.2, rows 4 and 19). `DataSourceId` is provenance and is not read.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "pm_crankcaseemissionratio": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-pm-exhaust/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__crankcaseemissionratio.parquet"
      },
      "reader_options": {
        "float_columns": [
          "crankcaseRatio"
        ]
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_crankcaseemissionratio"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "pm",
          "crankcase"
        ],
        "note": "572 rows, of which 20 reach this run: the four split species -- polProcessID 11201, 11501, 11901 and 12001, one per pollutant of sulfate_pm_calculator.rs's `CRANKCASE_SPLIT_POLLUTANTS` -- crossed with five (fuel type, model-year band) cells at source type 21 and regClass 20. THIS TABLE IS A ROW FILTER HERE AND NOT A MULTIPLY: every `crankcaseRatio` the run reaches is exactly 1.000000000000, so forcing the ratio to 1 changes none of the 1,456 cells, while removing the JOIN adds 40 electricity rows. It carries no fuel-type-9 row, which is the second of the two independent misses that empty those cohorts. The polProcessID is species x 100 + process, so the key is built with lib/identifiers.esm's `pol_process_id` and process 1's rows are selected by that key rather than by a filter -- process 15's exist in the table and this RunSpec does not select crankcase running exhaust. `crankcaseRatioCV` is a coefficient of variation and is not read.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "pm_pmspeciation": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-pm-exhaust/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__pmspeciation.parquet"
      },
      "reader_options": {
        "float_columns": [
          "pmSpeciationFraction"
        ]
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_pmspeciation"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "pm",
          "speciation"
        ],
        "note": "4 rows, every one `inputPollutantID` 120 -> `outputPollutantID` 111: the organic-carbon share of the internal residue. Gasoline and E85 take 0.706723639947 over all model years; DIESEL IS THE ONLY FUEL WITH TWO BANDS -- 0.725817529328 through 2006 and 0.741704256107 from 2007 -- which is the only reason the model-year predicate on this table is falsifiable at all (docs/process-pm-exhaust.md 7.2, row 20). The join keys on the OUTPUT pollutant as well as the input, so it both finds the fraction and identifies which rate rows are organic-carbon rows: pollutant 111 is named nowhere in this document (docs/esm-conventions.md 32.4). Because the table produces nothing but 111, NCOM (122), Total Organic Matter (123), NonECNonSO4NonOM (124) and the eleven trace metals and ions are reached by no emitted number.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    },
    "pm_pm10emissionratio": {
      "kind": "static",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "../../moves.rs/characterization/snapshots/process-pm-exhaust/tables/db__movesexecution1ccc0232_campuscluster_illinois_edu__pm10emissionratio.parquet"
      },
      "reader_options": {
        "float_columns": [
          "PM10PM25Ratio"
        ]
      },
      "extent": {
        "metaparameter": "n_pm10emissionratio"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "pm",
          "chain"
        ],
        "note": "4 rows, all polProcessID 10001, and the whole of `PM10EmissionCalculator` (pm10.rs::compute_pm10): PM10 total is PM2.5 total times `PM10PM25Ratio`, 1.130430 on fuel types 1, 5 and 9 and 1.086960 on fuel type 2, over one 1940-2060 band each. The polProcessID it carries is the OUTPUT one, so joining a rate row's own `polProcessID` to it both finds the ratio and identifies which rate rows are PM10 rows -- pollutant 100 is named nowhere in this document. TWO THINGS HERE ARE PRESENT AND UNREACHABLE: the fuel-type-9 row, because no PM2.5-total row survives to electricity, and the model-year band, because there is one band per (source type, fuel type). The Java's organic-carbon, elemental-carbon and sulfate PM10 branches (101 <- 111, 102 <- 112, 105 <- 115) are commented out in MOVES itself and are not ported. `PM10PM25RatioCV` is not read.",
        "esio_format": "parquet"
      }
    }
  },
