      "type": "integer",
      "default": 728,
      "description": "THE ONE DECLARED NUMBER IN THIS DOCUMENT: how many (pollutant-process, cohort) pairs reach MOVESOutput, over all seven pollutant-processes together. 728 = 7 x 104, and it is kept as ONE number with a GLOBAL rank over the rate relation (docs/esm-conventions.md 22 and 31) even though the blocks happen to be the same size here, because the rank costs nothing extra and a per-block offset would need every block to stay rectangular. WHICH rows emit is a result of the chain and is never written down: the rate relation carries 124 cohorts and every emitted block carries 104, because `sulfatefractions` has no fuel-type-9 row and `crankcaseemissionratio` has none either, and BOTH misses are computed because either alone would produce this row set. `run_outputRateRowCount` recomputes 728 from the chain and `pp_emittedCohortCount` recomputes the seven 104s against ONE shared cohort set -- 1,456 rows is equally consistent with 4 x 364 and with 8 x 182, and a row count cannot tell a seven-block set from a mis-shaped one."
    },
