          ],
          "description": "sulfatefractions.BaseFuelSulfurLevel: the sulfur level the base fraction was measured at -- 161.2, 23.5, 172.0 and 11.0 ppm -- and the DIVISOR of the adjustment. It is 0 on a cohort with no row, so `rt_baseFuelSulfurLevelGuarded` substitutes 1 there: 0/0 is NaN and 0 x NaN is NaN, so a miss has to be guarded with a VALUE and not with an indicator (docs/esm-conventions.md 29).",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "pm_sulfatefractions",
            "from": {
