        {
          "_comment": "The six pollutant-processes this chain names, each packed from MOVES's own constant and THIS ROW's process rather than written as a five-digit literal (lib/identifiers.esm's `pol_process_id`). Every one is a named constant in sulfate_pm_calculator.rs, which is the test docs/esm-conventions.md 32.4 sets: MOVES composes these species by IDENTITY -- `PM25_TOTAL_INPUTS` and `NON_EC_PM_INPUTS` are literal arrays of pollutant ids in the SQL -- so there is no table to look the composition up in. The two pollutants that DO have one, PM10 total and organic carbon, are named nowhere: `pm10emissionratio` and `pmspeciation` carry them and a join finds them. This one is unadjusted elemental carbon, `EC_POLLUTANT` -- one of the two RATED blocks and the parent of every EC term below.",
