          "_comment": "One formulation's contribution to the multiplier on a RATED block's base rate: its market share and the two fuel effects adjust.rs applies. `process-airtoxics` carried a third factor here, the speciation chain from the parent block to this row's own pollutant; this rung has no such factor, because its species are composed by summing spmOutput2 rather than by scaling the parent (`rtDay_quant`). Both remaining factors are per FORMULATION, so the product is formed before the market-share sum and not after -- the product of the means is not the mean of the products. It is indistinguishable in this county, where each fuel type is supplied by exactly one formulation at share 1.0, and docs/process-pm-exhaust.md 7.2 row 8 says so.",
