        {
          "_comment": "compute_sulfate_fractions' accumulation: SUM over the supplied formulations of marketShare x baseFraction x adjustment. The adjustment is per formulation and the base fraction is not, so the product is formed before the share sum -- indistinguishable here, where each fuel type is supplied by exactly one formulation at share 1.0, and docs/process-pm-exhaust.md 7.2 row 8 says so.",
          "lhs": "rt_sulfateFraction",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "args": [],
            "semiring": "sum_product",
            "output_idx": [
              "b"
            ],
            "ranges": {
              "b": {
