        {
          "_comment": "sulfate_pm_calculator.rs:636-639. THE SULFATE TAKES THE ADJUSTED FRACTION AND THE RESIDUE THE UNADJUSTED ONE, so the three species sum to 0.8385..0.9865 of the NonECPM they came from rather than to it. Using one fraction for both is wrong by 62 % on the 2007+ diesel sulfate block (docs/process-pm-exhaust.md 7.2, row 19). The `greatest(..., 0)` clamp is written and never binds -- the raw residue runs 0.26 to 0.95 -- and the gate on `rt_hasSulfateFractions` is load-bearing where the clamp is not: without it an unmatched cohort would take a residue fraction of 1 rather than 0.",
          "lhs": "rt_residueFraction",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "rt_hasSulfateFractions",
              {
                "op": "max",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "-",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "-",
                        "args": [
                          1.0,
                          "rt_waterFractionRaw"
                        ]
                      },
                      "rt_sulfateFractionRaw"
                    ]
                  },
                  0.0
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
