        {
          "_comment": "J53b, the SECOND instance of the same table under a different key. `SulfatePMCalculator.sql` 75 builds its extract with `gfr.pollutantID in (120)`, so only the internal residue is rescaled here -- the 11201 rows of the very same table were already applied one stage earlier by `BaseRateCalculator` (`rtSup_fuelFactor`). ../moves.rs records what merging them costs at sulfate_pm_calculator.rs:2226: it \"would wrongly rescale EC (and the PM2.5 total that sums it) -- e.g. process-pm-exhaust EC by ~1.09x on fuelType 1\". Two differences from the base-rate arm are written as written: this one joins on the fuel TYPE rather than the supplied FORMULATION, and it takes the raw ratio with NO GPA blend.",
