          "_comment": "lib/adjustments.esm's `exact_else_wildcard` under its second reading: not a regClass-0 fallback here but the multi-table UPDATE's own semantics, where the second arm is the multiplicative identity. Same shape, same template.",
          "lhs": "rt_residueFuelRatio",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "apply_expression_template",
            "args": [],
            "name": "exact_else_wildcard",
            "bindings": {
              "has_exact": {
                "op": ">",
                "args": [
                  "rt_hasResidueFuelRatio",
                  0.5
                ]
              },
              "exact_value": "rt_residueFuelRatioValue",
              "wildcard_value": 1.0
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "J52, and the whole of `PM10EmissionCalculator` (pm10.rs::compute_pm10): PM10 total is PM2.5 total times this ratio. Pollutant 100 is named NOWHERE in this document, because `pm10emissionratio.polProcessID` is the output pollutant-process and joining a rate row's own polProcessID to it identifies the PM10 rows and finds their ratio in one clause (docs/esm-conventions.md 32.4). The fuel-type-9 row is present and unreachable, and there is one model-year band per (source, fuel), so the band predicate is written and untested.",
          "lhs": "rt_pm10Ratio",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "args": [],
