        {
          "_comment": "J51, sulfate_pm_calculator.rs::speciate. FIVE key pairs, and two of them are doing different jobs: `inputPollutantID` pins the residue as the SOURCE species and `outputPollutantID` is matched against the rate row's OWN pollutant, so the lookup identifies which rate rows are organic-carbon rows -- pollutant 111 is named nowhere in this document either. Diesel is the only fuel with two model-year bands here, which is the only reason the band predicate is falsifiable (docs/process-pm-exhaust.md 7.2, row 20). The table produces nothing but 111, so NCOM, Total Organic Matter, NonECNonSO4NonOM and the eleven trace metals and ions are reached by no emitted number.",
