        {
          "_comment": "adjust.rs:105-110's PM ARM. Pollutant 112 and 118 on process 1 or 2 take the FIRST branch of `general_temp_adjust`, a MULTIPLICATIVE exponential exp(A x (72 - least(T, 72))), not the additive quadratic every earlier onroad rung took -- `process-airtoxics` reached the fall-through arm precisely because pollutant 1 \"is not 118/112 (PM)\", and this fixture is the other side of that sentence. The run is at 59.5 degF, so the T <= 72 half is the LIVE one; what makes the factor 1 is that `temperatureadjustment` has ZERO rows, so both arms of `exact_else_wildcard` miss and A is the additive identity. The arm has no B term, which is why this fixture computes only `rt_tempAdjustTermA`. Absent rather than inert, and swapping this branch for the quadratic changes no cell (docs/process-pm-exhaust.md 7.2, rows 1 and 2).",
