        {
          "_comment": "J54, and the shape this rung adds. `process-airtoxics` pulled ONE chain root onto each rate row; this fixture pulls TWO named parents, because five of the seven emitted pollutants are functions of both -- PM2.5 total is elemental carbon PLUS NonECPM, which no single-parent chain can express. Each is the same self-join on (the parent's polProcessID <-> this row's polProcessID, cohortOrdinal <-> cohortOrdinal), and on the parent's own row it selects that row's own quantity. There is no chain-root iteration here and no `rspp_rootPolProcessID`: `runspecchainedto` is cyclic (see `rspp_isChainOutput`), so the stages are written the way sulfate_pm_calculator.rs::calculate writes them.",
