          "description": "THE KEY-SET CLAIM, made in the document rather than in a comment. 1,456 rows is equally consistent with 4 x 364 and with 8 x 182, and the comparator's exact-key-set check would not separate a seven-block set from a mis-shaped one either, so the cohort count is asserted PER pollutant-process: 104 seven times, against one shared cohort set. `pp_selectedCohortCount` is 125, 125, 0, 125, 125, 125, 0 -- the two zeros are organic carbon and H2O aerosol, which MOVES never rates and for which it therefore writes no `pollutantprocessmodelyear` row, which is why the EMISSION test rides on the cohort relation. 125 - 1 rated - 20 = 104, and the 20 are lost twice over: no `sulfatefractions` fuel-9 row and no `crankcaseemissionratio` fuel-9 row. Three reach counts are pinned too: `criteriaratio` is EMPTY here and reaches 0 pairs, which is the mirror image of `process-airtoxics`, and `generalfuelratio` is live and reaches 67 (rate row, supplied formulation) pairs, every one of them on a RATED row.",
