        {
          "id": "the_crankcase_split_is_a_row_filter_and_not_a_multiply",
          "description": "All four species of `CRANKCASE_SPLIT_POLLUTANTS` looked up under their own polProcessID, at four key pairs and a model-year band. EVERY RATIO THE RUN REACHES IS EXACTLY 1: forcing them to 1 changes none of the 1,456 cells, while dropping the join adds 40 electricity rows, so the multiply is untested and the join is load-bearing (docs/process-pm-exhaust.md 7.2, rows 3 and 13). The presence half is the SECOND of the two independent fuel-9 misses -- `sulfatefractions` is the first -- and either alone would produce this row set, which is why both are computed. The lookups are separate because MOVES looks them up separately under four different keys; that they have identical fuel coverage here is a fact about the data.",
