        {
          "id": "the_general_fuel_ratio_enters_at_two_stages_on_two_pollutants",
          "description": "`criteriaratio` is EMPTY here and `generalfuelratio` is live, which is the reverse of `process-airtoxics`; and the live table's two pollutants enter at DIFFERENT stages. The polProcessID 11201 rows are the base-rate arm (adjust.rs:452-472): per SUPPLIED formulation, GPA-blended, and reaching only the elemental-carbon rate rows -- `rtSup_generalFuelRatio` is 1.090910749585 on gasoline from model year 2001 and 0.9727 on diesel through 2006, and 1 outside those bands. The 12001 rows are the `SulfatePMCalculator` arm (SulfatePMCalculator.sql 75): raw, on the fuel TYPE rather than the formulation, and as an UPDATE, so a miss is a factor of 1. Applying both to one quantity would SQUARE the 1.0909 on every gasoline and E85 cohort of 2001 or later; deleting either moves a cell by 8.3 % (docs/process-pm-exhaust.md 7.2, rows 15-17).",
