        {
          "id": "the_pm10_ratio_and_the_speciation_fraction_are_found_by_a_join_not_by_a_name",
          "description": "Two of the seven emitted pollutants are never named in this document. `pm10emissionratio.polProcessID` is 10001, the OUTPUT pollutant-process, so joining a rate row's own polProcessID to it both finds the ratio and says which rows are PM10 rows -- the lookup is 1.130430 on gasoline and E85 PM10 rows, 1.086960 on diesel ones, and exactly 0 on every other rate row in the relation. `pmspeciation` does the same job with `outputPollutantID`, matched against the rate row's pollutant while `inputPollutantID` pins the residue as the source: 0.706723639947 on gasoline and E85 organic-carbon rows, 0.741704256107 on 2007+ diesel ones, 0 elsewhere. The four SHARE columns then carry MOVES's whole composition of seven pollutants out of four species, with no branch on the pollutant: `PM25_TOTAL_INPUTS` is `rt_totalShare` in all four, `NON_EC_PM_INPUTS` is `rt_isNonECPM` in three, `COPIED_SPECIES` puts each of EC, sulfate and water in its own, and PM10 rides on the total at 1.13043.",
