        {
          "id": "the_two_parents_reach_every_rate_row_of_their_cohort_and_the_four_species_follow",
          "description": "J54, the shape this rung adds. Each parent is pulled onto every rate row of its cohort by a self-join on (the parent's polProcessID, cohortOrdinal), so `rtDay_ecQuant` and `rtDay_nonECQuant` carry the SAME two numbers on all seven blocks -- asserted at the elemental-carbon row, where one of them is the row's own quantity, and at the PM10 row, which has no rate of its own at all. Five of the seven emitted pollutants need both parents, which is why there are two pulls and not one chain. The four `spmOutput2` species then follow, and the numbers are MY 1980 gasoline on the weekend from docs/process-pm-exhaust.md 6.1: the residue is 0.92 of the parent while the sulfate is 0.0272 of it, and water is exactly 0.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
