          "description": "The three worked examples of docs/process-pm-exhaust.md 6.1-6.3, at all seven pollutants where they exist: MY 1980 gasoline on the weekend, MY 2020 gasoline on the weekday and MY 2010 diesel on the weekday, plus three MY 2020 E85 cells. output_rows is rate-major over the two day types, so an emitting rate row of rank r occupies positions 2r-1 (weekend) and 2r (weekday). The H2O aerosol cell is EXACTLY ZERO and its row exists, which is the kind of thing a row count finds and a sum does not. The diesel cells are the ones that carry the sulfate-heavy 2007+ band -- 0.5785 of the composite rather than 0.0665 -- and the 1.086960 PM10 ratio rather than 1.130430.",
